{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Factory Startup Data.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Factory Startup Data.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender factory startup data blender factory startup data","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Factory Startup Data.md","fileName":"Blender Factory Startup Data.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender Factory Startup Data","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-14 00:20\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Blender DNA and File Loading]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender DNA and File Loading","Blender Blend File Loading Pipeline","Blender Main Database","coreblenderdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Factory Startup Data.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Factory Startup Data.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender factory startup data blender factory startup data","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Factory Startup Data.md","fileName":"Blender Factory Startup Data.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender Factory Startup Data","heading":"Blender Factory Startup Data","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Blender's factory startup file is embedded into the executable as a byte array. During the build, the `datatoc` tool converts the repository's `startup.blend` into generated C source whose `datatoc_startup_blend` array preserves the original file bytes.\n\nAt application initialization, `WM_init()` selects this in-memory source for a factory start and sends it through the ordinary [[Blender Blend File Loading Pipeline]]. Embedding the data lets Blender reconstruct a known [[Blender Main Database]] without depending on an external startup file.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender DNA and File Loading","Blender Blend File Loading Pipeline","Blender Ma